  "term": "executive",
  "definition": "In psychology, executive usually refers to higher-order mental control processes involved in goal-directed behavior, self-regulation, and adapting to changing demands. These processes are commonly described in terms of inhibitory control, updating information in working memory, and cognitive flexibility.",
